Copyright (c) 2026 Bright Coast AI. All rights reserved.

This is a source-available licence, not an open source licence. The Materials are published in a public repository so that Bright Coast AI clients can download them in one click. Being able to see or download them does not, by itself, give you the right to use them.

1. What this covers

"Materials" means everything in this repository: the rules, the example page, the skill, the catalog, the scripts and the documents, and every copy of them. It does not include the things you make using them (sections 3(e) and 7).

2. Who may use the Materials

You are an "Authorised User" if any one of these is true:
(a) you, or the organisation you work for, are a client of Bright Coast AI (a current engagement, subscription or written agreement, including access to the Bright Coast AI client portal); or
(b) Bright Coast AI gave you the Materials, or a link to them, directly. For example: Rob Lee sent them to you, you received them in an email or message from Bright Coast AI, they were shared in a meeting, or you got them through the Bright Coast AI client portal; or
(c) Bright Coast AI has given you written permission. An email is enough.

If you only found the repository yourself, for example by searching the internet, you are not an Authorised User until one of the above is true. You may read the Materials, but you may not install, run, copy or use them. To ask for permission, write to support@brightcoast.ai.

3. What Authorised Users may do, free of charge

(a) Read the Materials.
(b) Install and run them on computers you own or control, for your own use or for the internal use of your own organisation.
(c) Let people in your own organisation use them the same way.
(d) Keep your own private edits and your own settings files for that use.
(e) Build what you find in the Materials into your own work. You may copy, adapt and combine any code sample, design rule, pattern, checklist or wording from the Materials into software, websites, apps, documents and other things you make, for your own use, for your organisation or for your customers, whether or not you sell them, as long as what you make is not itself the Materials, a copy of them, or a substitute for them.

4. What nobody may do without written permission from Bright Coast AI, Authorised Users included

(a) Republish or redistribute the Materials as such: the rules, the skill, the catalog, the example page, or a substantial part of them, on their own or as a collection, in a public or shared repository, template, course, marketplace, plugin, package or design-system product. Using pieces of them inside something you make under section 3(e) is not redistribution.
(b) Sell, rent, license or offer the Materials themselves, or a version of them with your changes, as a product or a service, or hand them to someone else as the thing they paid for. The test is whether the buyer is paying for the Materials or for what you built using them.
(c) Remove or change the copyright, credit or licence notices in the Materials themselves, or present the Materials as your own work. You do not need to add any credit to what you build under section 3(e).
(d) Use the Materials themselves to train, fine-tune or evaluate a machine learning model, or to build a product whose purpose is to be a competing library or set of design rules. What you build under section 3(e) is not covered by this.
(e) Change how the update mechanism works in order to distribute modified versions.

5. Your agreement with Bright Coast AI

If you are a client, the Materials are part of your engagement and section 3 applies to them. If your agreement with Bright Coast AI says something different about these Materials, your agreement wins.

6. Ideas are not covered

This licence covers the text and code of the Materials. It does not stop you from having, using or writing about your own ideas, or from building your own tools from scratch that do similar jobs.

7. What you make is yours

Anything you make using the Materials belongs to you, including code and text you copied or adapted from them under section 3(e). Ending this licence does not take back anything you already built into your work.

8. Other people's tools

Some Materials mention or point to tools made by other people. Those tools have their own licences and their own risks. This licence gives you no rights to them, and Bright Coast AI does not vouch for them.

9. No warranty

THE MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT THE LAW ALLOWS, BRIGHT COAST AI IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGE OR LOSS ARISING FROM THE MATERIALS OR THEIR USE.

10. Ending

Your rights under this licence end automatically if you break it. Bright Coast AI may also end them by telling you in writing. When they end, stop using the Materials and delete your copies.

11. Permission and questions

To ask for permission to do something this licence does not allow, or to ask anything about it, write to support@brightcoast.ai.

